cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the article it accompanies."
type: software
title: "aspir-edge-deploy: deployment and measurement code for quantised U-Net single-pixel imaging denoising on the Ultra96-V2 DPU and the Jetson Orin NX"
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Xarlie123/aspir-edge-deploy"
abstract: >-
  Single-pixel imaging forms an image with one detector, in an acquisition
  time that grows with the number of projected patterns. Fewer patterns
  shorten acquisition but degrade the reconstruction; a learned denoiser
  recovers that quality at a fixed computational cost. The accompanying
  article deploys a compact U-Net denoiser, in a simulated pipeline, on two
  edge platforms, a Vitis AI DPU soft accelerator in the reconfigurable logic
  of an Avnet Ultra96-V2 and TensorRT on the embedded GPU of an NVIDIA Jetson
  Orin NX, and measures quality, quantisation fidelity, latency and energy per
  frame over seven sensing configurations and two image classes, beams and
  faces.

  This repository holds the code behind that deployment and those
  measurements: eight-bit quantisation and compilation for the DPU, with the
  fourteen compiled models; the DPU overlay as measured (block design,
  constraints, hardware export, bitstream and implementation reports);
  TensorRT engine builds; the CPU, DPU and GPU runners with their power
  sampling, and the sweep matrices; pinned environments for the host and both
  boards; and the pipeline that regenerates the article's tables and figures
  from the companion dataset, aspir-edge-data.
